// Flow-sensitive reads (DECISIONS.md, "A read of a `let` takes its most recent write's type"):
// a read of a `let x = null` before the write that fills it is `null`, delivered at every
// position into a `string | null`, and the fill after it (in the proof) makes the binding
// `i32 | null`. D2660 is the generic-call row of this grid. The proof prints the filled
// binding's value when the delivered one is null, else -1.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@SETUP@@
let x = null
// @@VALUE@@
x
// @@TYPE@@
string | null
// @@PROOF@@
x = 5
if v == null { print(x ?? 0) } else { print(-1) }
// @@WANT@@
5
